{"seq":4,"id":"01M6M7V24NW67Z4F3W2V1A7JNB","cdr":"CDR-0005","attempt":"CDR-0005-A1","type":"agent.result","actor":{"kind":"agent","id":"test_author","adapter":"claude"},"at":"2026-11-04T21:36:01.685Z","payload":{"role":"test_author","adapter":"claude","result_sha256":"6c190bec92b77cfebc589274e097834f23b4d41ec0223284f065c8fea5f7ff73","result":{"tests":[{"path":"internal/makefilecheck/makefile_cdr0005_test.go","covers_criterion":"A file named Makefile exists at the repository root. (TestMakefileExistsAtRoot)"},{"path":"internal/makefilecheck/makefile_cdr0005_test.go","covers_criterion":"`make -n test` prints `go test ./...`. (TestMakeTestPrintsGoTest)"},{"path":"internal/makefilecheck/makefile_cdr0005_test.go","covers_criterion":"`make -n vet` prints `go vet ./...`. (TestMakeVetPrintsGoVet)"},{"path":"internal/makefilecheck/makefile_cdr0005_test.go","covers_criterion":"`make -n` with no target prints both `go vet ./...` and `go test ./...`. (TestMakeDefaultPrintsVetAndTest)"},{"path":"internal/makefilecheck/makefile_cdr0005_test.go","covers_criterion":"The test and vet targets are declared .PHONY. (TestTestAndVetArePhony)"}],"run_command":"go test ./internal/makefilecheck/","notes":"I haven't run these tests. On the current code they should all fail because there is no Makefile at the repository root.\n\n- **Location:** The tests are in a new directory that holds only tests, `internal/makefilecheck`. I put them there so they can't clash with the root package's name.\n- **Finding the root:** The tests find the repository root by walking up from the test's directory until they reach `go.mod`.\n- **How they run make:** They need `make` on PATH. They run `make -n [target]` from the root and require exit code 0. Each output line is trimmed of leading and trailing whitespace and must equal `go test ./...` or `go vet ./...` exactly.\n- **Recipe lines:** Write the recipes literally. Don't use variables like `$(GO)`, because `make -n` prints the expanded command and that would only pass if `GO=go`. Don't use leading `@` or `-` either.\n- **Default target:** The first target in the file, for example `all: vet test`, must run both commands.\n- **.PHONY check:** This test reads the Makefile text. `test` and `vet` must appear on one or more `.PHONY:` lines; backslash line continuations are fine.\n- **Makefile content:** Your Makefile must not run `go test ./...` with an extra flag, because `make -n` would then print a line the test doesn't match."}},"cost":{"tokens_in":8,"tokens_out":3253,"seconds":35.7906885,"usd":0.14073760000000002},"signer":"ads-team:marcello.barile@gmail.com","prev_hash":"b94168f3606ccfdb15ffbb52e33a66f44ebb8e3b7bec138529f7d1f0730b17f9","hash":"a9300b2674e20e7c52048f3a811d34593582e08a9147b9a189a73f99c548df20","sig":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgt+9LVHCb4CLBAIrBcP4iIkhhc+\nSCDbAr1oNRi9kG2bAAAAAJYWRzLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1l\nZDI1NTE5AAAAQE6gKelRusu54ujhFxogAcHPPhyneSxbl5d7cUGgpIpBDM53irxBLvGuB9\nb9TtpRrD7N8sz9YxpS08QOYITHgQs=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----\n"}
